## 1. FFmpeg — no longer bundled

| | |
|---|---|
| Status | **Removed on 2026-10-14** |
| Was | `packages/server/bin/ffmpeg` — FFmpeg 9.0.1, `tessus` static macOS build |
| Licence of the removed file | **GNU General Public License** (built with `--enable-gpl --enable-version3`) |

The file was deleted for two independent reasons:

1. It was an **x86_64** binary. On Apple Silicon it fails with
   `bad CPU type in executable`, so it was never a usable fallback on the platforms
   this project targets.
2. Shipping a GPL build triggers the GPL's redistribution conditions for that binary
   (corresponding source, licence text travelling with it). That is a poor trade for
   a fallback that does not work on the target platform in the first place.

FFmpeg is now resolved at runtime from the user's own installation:
`ffmpegPath` setting → `PATH` → `~/.supercrzy/bin` → common package-manager paths.
The resolver and its install guidance live in
`packages/server/src/services/ffmpeg.ts`; the regression guard is
`packages/server/src/services/ffmpeg.test.ts`.

**The licence of the user's own FFmpeg build is the user's choice and responsibility.**
The install hint deliberately does not recommend any particular third-party prebuilt
package for this reason.

