## 2. Agent Skills — vendored from Anthropic

Directory: `packages/server/.agents/skills/`
Upstream: https://github.com/anthropics/skills — commit `f6656c12` (2026-08-13)

### 2a. Document skills — removed (were proprietary)

`docx`, `pdf`, `pptx` and `xlsx` were **removed on 2026-10-14**.

Upstream marks these files `license: Proprietary. LICENSE.txt has complete terms`, and
its README describes the set as *"source-available, not open source"*. The additional
restrictions in their `LICENSE.txt` prohibit extracting the materials, reproducing
them, creating derivative works from them, and distributing them to third parties —
so they could not be vendored in this repository.

Worth recording for anyone auditing history: the local copies had already lost
upstream's `license:` field and never shipped the `scripts/` they reference, so they
were simultaneously unauthorised **and** non-functional. The root cause was in this
codebase rather than in the upstream files —

- `installSkillFromGitHub` wrote only the `SKILL.md` text to the database and then
  deleted the whole clone, so `scripts/`, `references/` and `LICENSE.txt` were lost;
- `exportSkillToFile` rebuilt frontmatter from database columns, which have no
  `license` field.

Both are fixed: the installer now copies the entire skill directory, and the exporter
preserves an existing `license:` line. Regression tests cover both.

If you need document support, install such a skill from upstream yourself using the
built-in installer — the licence terms then travel with the files into your own
installation — or use an independent implementation. **Do not re-vendor these files
into this repository.**

### 2b. Apache-2.0 skills

Twelve skills are vendored under the **Apache License 2.0**:

`algorithmic-art`, `brand-guidelines`, `canvas-design`, `claude-api`,
`frontend-design`, `internal-comms`, `mcp-builder`, `skill-creator`,
`slack-gif-creator`, `theme-factory`, `web-artifacts-builder`, `webapp-testing`

Each directory carries upstream's `LICENSE.txt` alongside its `SKILL.md`, satisfying
Apache-2.0 §4(a). Both files are **byte-identical to upstream** (verified by md5), so
no §4(b) modification notice is required.

### 2c. Skills with no upstream licence file — removed

`doc-coauthoring` and `template-skill` were **removed on 2026-10-14**. Upstream ships no
`LICENSE.txt` for either, so their terms were unclear; `template-skill` was additionally
still unfilled placeholder text (`Replace with description of the skill...`). Nothing here
should be redistributed without clear terms, so both were dropped rather than shipped with
an open question attached.

As a result, **every** skill under `.agents/skills/` now has a determinate licence:
12 under Apache-2.0 (see 2b) and 3 authored by this project (see 2d).

### 2d. Project-authored skills

`computer-use`, `content-pipeline` and `skill-finder` are written by this project and
are covered by the MIT grant in `LICENSE`.

