## 5. Third-party services contacted at runtime

This is not a licence grant, and it is recorded here because users should know what the
software talks to on their behalf.

**Speech synthesis (Pro voice).** The read-aloud feature does **not** use a documented,
licensed public API. It calls an internal Microsoft Edge "Read Aloud" endpoint using the
protocol the Edge browser itself uses. That endpoint is **not offered for third-party
consumption**, has no terms permitting this use, and may change or stop working at any
time. If you need speech synthesis you can depend on, use a commercial provider
(for example Azure Speech, which serves the same neural voices under a real SLA) and
treat the current implementation as a convenience fallback.

Other network calls are made to the model providers you configure yourself, and to those
providers' endpoints only.

